@spec mm_sidecar_state_spec  src=tests/specs/mm_sidecar_state_spec.lua  loc=211  sha=untracked  cases=5
@exercises midiManager (h.mm)
@surface   mm:notes, mm:ccs, mm:load, mm:modify, mm:delete, mm:assign, mm:add
@harness   fakeReaper:bindTake

# Intent
  Phase 2d of stable-slots: the sidecar rows stop being regenerated per flush and
  become mm state the verbs maintain. The pin is equivalence -- a storm of gestures on
  a live instance must serialise to exactly the bytes a fresh wholesale load of the
  same take produces. A missed drop leaves a dead row behind (on a reused slot, one
  wearing the wrong body); a missed put loses one. Either diverges.

# Helpers
  @fn freshTake()  @ 10-16
  @fn captureBlobs(rp)  @ 20-27
      -- Every blob that reaches the take, in order: the storm's flush and the wholesale
      -- instance's flush are the two the equivalence pin compares.
  @fn noteOfPitch(mm, pitch)  @ 29-31
  @fn noteAtPpq(mm, ppq)  @ 33-35
  @fn ccAtPpq(mm, ppq)  @ 37-39
  @fn rdmRows(rp, take)  @ 41-47
  @fn notationRows(rp, take)  @ 51-58
      -- The notation rows as the take holds them, in wire order: { ppq, pitch } is enough to
      -- tell a dropped row from a lingering one and a moved row from a stale one.

# Cases
  @case 'a gesture storm serialises exactly like a wholesale rebuild of the same take'  [pure]  @ 65-115
  @case 'a deleted note takes its notation row with it; the survivor keeps its own'  [pure]  @ 119-137
  @case 'a backstop kill takes the loser\'s notation row with it'  [pure]  @ 143-161
  @case 'a backstop nudge carries the notation row to the new onset'  [pure]  @ 165-183
  @case 'a metadata-bearing cc gets its }RDM row on the spot, promoted or added'  [pure]  @ 189-209

# Uses (outbound edges)
  @use call mm:notes  @ 30,34,157
  @use call mm:ccs  @ 38
